.TH CRU 1 "August 2026" "Cruine 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cru \- Android Custom ROM build automation engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cru
.RI <destination>
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B cru
.RI <command>
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cru
automates the complete Android Custom ROM build pipeline. It scans the
current working directory for a
.B rc.json
recipe, pulls the ROM manifest and device source trees, configures the
lunch target, executes the build, and packages the output into an archive
at the requested destination.
.PP
The ROM manifest is synced by Cruine's native sync engine: it parses AOSP
.I repo
manifest XML directly and clones every active project with plain
.BR git .
No
.B repo
binary is required. Any URL form works (https, ssh, git,
.BR file:// ,
scp-style
.IR git@host:path ,
or a plain local path) and any revision can be requested (branch, tag, or
SHA-1). Unchanged projects are skipped on repeat runs via state kept in
.IR <workspace>/.cruine .
.PP
Sources may come from the network or from local git repositories: a
.B file://
URL (or a plain filesystem path) for the manifest or any device tree is
initialized/cloned without network access.
.PP
Cruine can also repack an existing ROM archive. When the recipe defines an
.B input.archive
(or when
.B cru repack
is used), the archive is extracted into the product tree, the recipe's
patches and hooks run, and the result is re-archived. Extraction is
path-traversal safe.
.PP
The tool supports two invocation styles:
.TP
.B Legacy pipeline
.B cru /path/to/output
runs the full pipeline (discover recipe, validate environment, fetch
sources, build, package) against a destination directory. This is the
classic single-command workflow.
.TP
.B Command tree
.B cru <command>
dispatches into a deep command tree of groups and functional commands.
Run
.B cru help
or
.BR "cru tree" .
.SH LEGACY OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-r,\ \-\-recipe " FILE"
Path to a non-standard recipe file (default:
.BR ./rc.json ).
.TP
.BI \-w,\ \-\-work-dir " PATH"
Build workspace directory (default:
.IR <cwd>/<project_name> ).
.TP
.BI \-j,\ \-\-jobs " N"
Number of parallel build jobs (overrides the recipe option).
.TP
.BI \-v,\ \-\-verbose
Enable verbose (debug) logging.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colors.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Validate the recipe and print the execution plan without running anything.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-fetch ", " \-\-no\-fetch
Skip source fetching and use the existing tree.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-package
Build but do not package the outputs.
.TP
.B \-\-clean
Force a clean build
.RB ( "mka clean" ).
.TP
.BI \-\-mem\-limit " MB"
Enforce a virtual-memory ulimit during the build.
.TP
.BI \-g,\ \-\-generate-template " PATH"
Write an example
.B rc.json
recipe and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-formats
List supported output archive formats and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the Cruine version and exit.
.SH COMMAND TREE
The tree mixes letter groups and functional commands. Each group contains
member commands; almost every command has aliases (see
.BR "cru help" ).
.SS Functional commands
.TP
.B build
Build the ROM via the full pipeline.
.TP
.B init
Write an example
.B rc.json
recipe.
.TP
.B config
Show the active recipe configuration.
.TP
.B doctor
Validate the host environment and tools. Required: git, bash, tar,
python3, make, java, javac (a full JDK, not a bare JRE). Warns about common
AOSP/Kernel build tools (clang, clang++, gcc, g++, bison, flex, ...) and
optional fallbacks, and reports the detected libc/toolchain profile (Cudane:
musl + clang/clang++, target triple <arch>-unknown-linux-musl; glibc: gcc/g++,
<arch>-unknown-linux-gnu) plus the JDK version against the usual AOSP targets.
.TP
.B info
Print the build plan for the active recipe.
.TP
.B fetch
Pull manifests and device trees.
.TP
.B patch
Apply recipe patches.
.TP
.B pack
Package build outputs.
.B \-\-source
packages an arbitrary directory (e.g. an extracted ROM);
.B \-\-format
overrides the recipe format.
.TP
.B extract
Extract a ROM archive into a directory. Positional
.I archive
plus an optional
.B \-o/\-\-output
target; the default output directory is the archive name without its suffix.
Supports
.BR .zip ,
.BR .tar ,
.BR .tar.gz ,
.BR .tar.bz2 ,
.BR .tar.xz ,
.BR .tgz ,
.BR .7z .
.TP
.B repack
Extract a ROM archive into the product tree, run the recipe's patches and
hooks, and re-archive it. Positionals:
.I archive
and an optional
.IR destination .
.B \-\-format
overrides the output format.
.TP
.B clean
Request a clean build.
.TP
.B formats
List supported output formats.
.TP
.B version
Print Cruine version.
.TP
.B env
Show host environment report.
.TP
.B log
Tail most recent build log.
.TP
.B ccache
Inspect ccache statistics.
.TP
.B jobs
Print recommended parallel job count.
.TP
.B path
Resolve and echo a command path.
.TP
.B tree
Print command tree.
.TP
.B help
Show help for a command or path.
.TP
.B tier
Deep command chain (depth 25).
.TP
.B crush
Interactive shell over the command tree.
.SS Group commands
The letters
.B a
through
.B z
and
.B A
through
.B Z
are command groups (analytics, builder, control, device, engine, fetch, ...).
Each member command exposes subcommands and a deep planet chain; inspect a
group with
.BR "cru a" .
