.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRUINE_CONFIG
Path to the user config file (default
.BR ~/.config/cruine/config.toml ).
.TP
.B CRU_JOBS
Parallel job count; overrides the recipe and CLI
.BR \-j .
.TP
.B USE_CCACHE
Set to 1 when ccache is enabled by the recipe.
.TP
.B CCACHE_EXEC
Path to the ccache binary used during the build.
.TP
.B CCACHE_DIR
ccache cache directory (default
.BR ~/.cache/ccache ).
.TP
.B LC_ALL ", " LANG
Forced to
.B C
during builds for stable output.
.SH BUILDING
Cruine is built with Make, Ninja, Meson, or CMake. All share the host-profile
detector
.B scripts/detect.sh
(musl/Cudane vs glibc), which selects the install prefix
.BR /system
(Cudane) or
.BR /usr
(glibc), and the toolchain
.BR "clang/clang++" " (musl, targets " "x86_64/aarch64-unknown-linux-musl") "
or
.BR "gcc/g++" " (glibc, targets " "x86_64/aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu") ".
.PP
.nf
make build && make install            # Make (prefix via env.mk)
ninja && ninja install                # Ninja (DESTDIR honored)
meson setup build && meson install -C build   # Meson (-Dprefix=... honored)
.fi
.PP
Other build files:
.RS
.IP \[bu] 2
env.mk, build.ninja, meson.build, scripts/cross.sh (Meson cross-file),
toolchain.cmake (CMake), scripts/pkgconfig.sh (pkg-config wrapper),
scripts/package.sh (PyInstaller build shared by Make/Ninja/Meson),
packaging/cru.spec (PyInstaller spec).
.RE
.PP
Overrides:
.B CRUINE_LIBC
(force musl/glibc),
.B CRUINE_PREFIX
(force install prefix),
.B CC
and
.B CXX
(force the compiler pair).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Cruine reads an optional user config from
.B ~/.config/cruine/config.toml
(overridable with the
.B CRUINE_CONFIG
environment variable). It controls all output formatting: the log line
format, the timestamp pattern, per-status labels and colours, and the
program name used by the
.B {program}
variable.
.PP
Log lines default to
.B "[HH:MM:SS] [Status] message"
with the status capitalised and colourised. Any format string is accepted;
placeholders such as
.BR {ts} ", " {time} ", " {date} ", " {status} ", " {label} ", " {level} ", "
.BR {message} ", " {msg} ", " {program} ", " {pid} ", " {hostname} ", "
.BR {counter} ", " {elapsed} ", " {color} ", " {reset} ", " {bold} " and " {dim}
are supported. Unknown placeholders render empty; an empty format prints
bare messages.
.PP
Over 200 named statuses ship with the logger (for example
.BR Info ", " Ok ", " Warn ", " Error ", " Fatal ", " Build ", " Fetch ", "
.BR Sync ", " Patch ", " Pack ", " Extract ", " Verify ", " Retry ", "
.B Timeout
and
.BR Missing ).
.PP
.nf
[general]
program = "cru"

[log]
format = "[{ts}] [{color}{status}{reset}] {message}"
timestamp_format = "%H:%M:%S"
verbose = false
no_color = false

[log.statuses]
Build = { label = "BUILDING", color = "bright_blue" }
.fi
.PP
Manage the config from the CLI:
.BR "cru config" " (show), " "cru config reload" ", " "cru config path" ", "
.B "cru config init"
(writes an example to
.BR ~/.config/cruine/config.toml ;
.B --dir PATH
writes it into a chosen directory instead).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B rc.json
The active recipe; discovered in the current directory.
.TP
.B ~/.config/cruine/config.toml
Optional user configuration (see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
.TP
.I <project_name>\-build.log
Build log written next to the destination.
.TP
.B ~/.cru_history
Shell command history (used by
.BR "cru crush" ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error (missing recipe, build failure, packaging failure, ...).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown command, unknown option).
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (SIGINT).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run the full pipeline to a destination directory:
.nf
cru /home/user/build_outputs
.fi
.TP
Dry-run with an explicit recipe:
.nf
cru /home/user/build_outputs --recipe ./recipes/pixel.json --dry-run
.fi
.TP
Use the command tree:
.nf
cru info
cru doctor
cru build --skip-fetch --clean -j 16
cru log --dir /var/log/rom
cru tree 3
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rc.json (5),
.BR crush (1)
